  "rationale": "Re-recorded against the merged tree. The previous file measured a build 85 commits older and was invalid on provenance the moment this branch merged main, so this is a first real baseline rather than a movement claim; the deltas below are two builds apart and are not a regression signal. Why this sweep exists: the two cheap gates play no god verb at all. passive-control declares signatureActions [] and preferences () => [], so the fall-through submits noop on every tick, and between them balance:gate and balance:gate:horizon contain zero god interventions across 400 runs -- no change to any of the fifteen verbs in coordination/src/god/interventions.ts can move either by construction. That is not a tolerance problem and no statistic fixes it. Until now the only committed gate that put a strategy in front of the verbs was the 200-year ascension sweep, which on this build costs about 830 seconds. This one is the horizon gate's twenty-year cap with the ascension gate's eight-strategy round-robin pool -- the single declared difference from balance-gate-horizon-v1 is the pool, so a divergence between them is attributable to god agency and to nothing else, and horizon-gate.test.ts asserts that rather than describing it.",
